finalDraft.description:
Why: Decision #9 — Print is a `<button>` with a `window.print()` handler. The handler lives in the Newsroom site clientlib's JS so it loads on every press-release page.

What: In the Newsroom clientlib JS (T-006), add a small handler:
```
document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
  const btn = e.target.closest('[data-print-trigger]');
  if (btn) { e.preventDefault(); window.print(); }
});
```
Wire the JS file into the clientlib's `js.txt`. Use event delegation so multiple share rows on a page (unlikely but possible) all work.

Edge cases: handler must be idempotent (no duplicate listeners). No external print-service URL, no dedicated print view.

